.page wallpaper 1 set the desktop picture

# SYNOPSIS
*wallpaper* [*-m* _MODE_] _IMAGE_
*wallpaper* *-c*
*wallpaper*

# DESCRIPTION
`wallpaper` chooses the picture behind the windows. The choice is stored in *~/.config/hakurei/wallpaper* (first line: the full path of the picture, second line: the mode), and the desktop notices the change within a second or two and redraws. The picture is decoded once and scaled to the size of the screen; the original is not kept in memory.

Without arguments it prints the current setting. If the picture cannot be read, or the file is later removed, the desktop falls back to the built-in night scene (the moon, the torii and the bamboo). The login screen uses the system-wide setting in */etc/hakurei/wallpaper* if there is one, since nobody is signed in yet.

# OPTIONS
@ *-m* _MODE_
    How the picture fills the screen: *cover* (the default: fill the screen and crop what sticks out), *fit* (show all of it, with night-blue bars), *center* (original size, cropped or surrounded by bars), *tile* (repeat it) or *stretch* (fill the screen and ignore the proportions). Without *-m* the mode that was set before is kept.
@ *-c*
    Remove the setting and go back to the built-in scene.

# EXIT STATUS
0, 1 if the picture cannot be read or the setting cannot be saved, 2 for bad usage.

# EXAMPLES
    wallpaper ~/Pictures/moon.jpg
    wallpaper -m tile pattern.png
    wallpaper -c

# SEE ALSO
gallery(1), imginfo(1), screenshot(1)
